# Requirements Gathering

When creating or updating requirements documents (Builder Brief, Conventional PRD, specs) and you need input from the user:

## Behavior

- **Ask one item at a time.** Don't ask for "project name, goal, and problem" in one go. Ask for project name. Wait. Build on that. Then ask for goal. Wait. Then problem/opportunity.
- **Build on each answer.** Use what they said to shape the next question. "You said [X] — what's the immediate goal that would address that?"
- **Wait for response before scaffolding.** Don't fill in placeholders until you have their answers. The document emerges from the conversation.
- **Group related items into sub-themes** only after you've gathered enough to see the themes.

## Applies To

- create-builder-brief
- requirement-agent (create/update PRD)
- Any spec or requirements doc that needs user input

## Complements

Works with the conversational-flow rule. This rule adds requirements-specific behavior on top of the general "one question at a time" norm.
